      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenSRE is an open-source toolkit that helps site reliability engineers automate incident management using AI agents. It connects to monitoring platforms like Datadog and Grafana to analyze alerts, identify root causes, and suggest remediation steps through natural language processing. Developers can customize these AI agents with Python to handle specific infrastructure patterns, deploy them via Slack integrations, and reduce manual troubleshooting time during system outages.",
        "zh": "OpenSRE是一个开源工具包，旨在通过AI代理帮助站点可靠性工程师自动化事件管理流程。它连接Datadog、Grafana等监控平台，利用自然语言处理技术分析告警、定位根因并推荐修复方案。开发者可用Python定制这些AI代理来处理特定基础设施模式，通过Slack集成部署，从而在系统故障时减少人工排查时间，提升运维效率。",
        "es": "OpenSRE is an open-source toolkit that helps site reliability engineers automate incident management using AI agents. It connects to monitoring platforms like Datadog and Grafana to analyze alerts, identify root causes, and suggest remediation steps through natural language processing. Developers can customize these AI agents with Python to handle specific infrastructure patterns, deploy them via Slack integrations, and reduce manual troubleshooting time during system outages.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "opensre stands out for ai-sre, alerting, and datadog in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "OpenSRE is an open-source toolkit that helps site reliability engineers automate incident management using AI agents. It connects to monitoring platforms like Datadog and Grafana to analyze alerts, identify root causes, and suggest remediation steps through natural language processing. Developers can customize these AI agents with Python to handle specific infrastructure patterns, deploy them via Slack integrations, and reduce manual troubleshooting time during system outages.",
